HISTORICAL / PARTIAL: read MISTAKE-237 and HYP-8905; only the binary homogeneous formula survives.
======================================================================
[1] Binary family P=A z^d+B zbar^d: nilpotent Hessian iff A*B=0
======================================================================
  d=3 A=1 B=0 [holomorphic (one-sided) ]: trace=9.70e-11 det=7.34e-11 -> nilpotent=True
  d=3 A=0 B=1 [antiholo (one-sided)    ]: trace=1.19e-08 det=1.87e-08 -> nilpotent=True
  d=3 A=1 B=1 [TWO-sided               ]: trace=2.27e-08 det=1.56e+01 -> nilpotent=False
  d=4 A=1 B=0 [holomorphic (one-sided) ]: trace=4.00e-08 det=8.62e-12 -> nilpotent=True
  d=4 A=0 B=1 [antiholo (one-sided)    ]: trace=4.10e-08 det=5.71e-08 -> nilpotent=True
  d=4 A=1 B=1 [TWO-sided               ]: trace=7.58e-08 det=6.74e+00 -> nilpotent=False
  d=5 A=1 B=0 [holomorphic (one-sided) ]: trace=3.23e-08 det=4.58e-13 -> nilpotent=True
  d=5 A=0 B=1 [antiholo (one-sided)    ]: trace=1.32e-07 det=5.04e-08 -> nilpotent=True
  d=5 A=1 B=1 [TWO-sided               ]: trace=1.55e-07 det=2.02e+00 -> nilpotent=False
  => inside this binary family only, nilpotence occurs exactly when A*B=0.

======================================================================
[2] one-sided map F=(x,y)+grad P is ONE-FIBER-LINEAR (F2 - i F1 = -i z), hence TAME/invertible
======================================================================
  point z=-0.100+0.100j: F2 - i F1 = 0.1000+0.1000j  vs  -i z = 0.1000+0.1000j  (match => linear pencil member)
  point z=0.500+0.000j: F2 - i F1 = 0.0000-0.5000j  vs  -i z = 0.0000-0.5000j  (match => linear pencil member)

======================================================================
[3] Zhao VC / moment: one-sided P is HARMONIC (holomorphic), Delta=0, so Delta^m(P^m)=0 trivially
======================================================================
  Delta((x+iy)^3) = 9.70e-11  (=0: holomorphic is harmonic => Delta^m(P^m)=0, Zhao VC trivial one-sided)
  Delta((x+iy)^4) = 4.00e-08  (=0: holomorphic is harmonic => Delta^m(P^m)=0, Zhao VC trivial one-sided)

